    fn flush() -> Future<Result<(), IoError>>:
        """Flush write buffer."""
        Future(state: [], poll_result: Poll.Ready(self.stream.flush()))  # @workaround bug=mir-unresolved-method-20261031 reason=pinned stage2 MIR lowers the generic Future.from_value<T> callee body with T unsubstituted (E-MIR-TYPE-TypeParam, unaffected by explicit call-site type args); construct the Future record directly, identical to from_value's own body

    me close() -> Future<Result<(), IoError>>:
